## Recovery (each is YELLOW and needs its own GO)
- Window left open / session lost: `bash scripts/d1-migrate-prd.sh --restore-only` (verifies the security group equals the recorded original).
- Migration failed part-way: STOP; do not deploy. The failing file rolled back; earlier files stay applied. Fix forward (never edit an applied file), then `migrate --resume`. Or roll back (below).
- Web wrong: `bash scripts/d3-web-prd.sh rollback-verify` then `rollback` (phrase `RESTORE-WEB-Ogevia-prd`): restores the captured files and `index.html`, verifies against the capture.
- API wrong: quick rollback `aws lambda update-function-code --function-name <handler> --s3-bucket <bucket> --s3-key <previous key>` from `~/ogevia-prd-before/previous-api-asset.txt`, then reconcile the CloudFormation drift with a reviewed redeploy. (This is NOT scripted here; the previous asset was verified to exist at baseline.)
- Database: `bash scripts/d1-migrate-prd.sh rollback` (phrases `OPEN-5432-WINDOW-ROLLBACK-PRD` and `ROLLBACK-DROPS-DATA-ogevia_prd`). 13 of the 39 down scripts DROP TABLES WITH THEIR ROWS; the pre-release snapshot is the only backup and **restoring a snapshot is not a prepared procedure**. Roll the API and web back as well (the old API needs the old schema).

## Not verified before the first real run (be ready for these)
- Everything in AWS: the security-group edit, the Session Manager tunnel, the RDS-managed secret read, the CDK deploy, the S3 upload and CloudFront invalidation have never run; the mocks emulate the calls the scripts make, not AWS's behavior.
- The migrations ran against PostgreSQL 16 (local), not the RDS instance's PostgreSQL 18.3; they ran on a restored copy of production (rehearsal R4-R6, PostgreSQL 18.3) with the same files.
- Whether a CloudShell `cdk synth` reproduces the pinned asset hashes (it did in the development container; the assembly check stops the release if not).
- Whether the live production bundle embeds the same Cognito/API values the build reuses (the build stops and prints any difference).
- The 1-2 minute window between the migration and the API deploy is an estimate.
